# On-prem pack gates

When packing, upgrading packs, or touching on-prem web build:

1. **Ship the fix in the artifact**, not only in docs. If §3.1 / handoff names a Dockerfile or migrate ensure, it must already be in the tree **before** `pack-release.sh`.
2. `pack-release.sh` hard-fails without:
   - **Tip baseline / covered = all migrations** (`baseline_covered_migrations.txt` lists every `supabase/migrations/*.sql` → fresh-install **pending=0**). If pending>0: run `./deploy/on-prem/scripts/export-schema-baseline.sh` on a tip green DB, then pack. Do **not** ship “old baseline + long pending stack” as the install path.
   - **Live upgrade must not stamp covered:** `apply-migrations.sh` with `MESA_MIGRATE_INCREMENTAL_ONLY=1` only runs ledger-missing `*.sql` — never `sync_covered_from_file` (that skips SQL; Pirata 2026-10-21). Covered stamp only right after a fresh tip baseline dump.
   - `schema/ensure_realtime_publication.sql` + `apply-migrations` call
   - `apps/web/Dockerfile`: `RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.npm npm ci`
   - `apps/web/Dockerfile`: do **not** default `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRINT_AGENT_GITHUB_REPO` to a repo (empty ARG) so on-prem hides the download card via `getPrintAgentDownloadUrls()===null`; do **not** `COPY apps/print-agent/VERSION` (recommended agent = Fiscal Agent via env pin or GitHub `fiscal-agent-v*`)
   - `apps/web/Dockerfile` + `compose.yaml` + `upgrade.sh` / `install-mesa.sh`: `MESA_WEB_VERSION` (web build id for `/api/health/live` + settings footer via `getWebAppBuildInfo`)
3. Do not tell the user “docs say use BuildKit cache” while shipping a pack with bare `RUN npm ci`.
4. **Same-origin flag:** never `menuImageSameOriginEnabled(process.env)` — Next will not inline nested `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`; call `menuImageSameOriginEnabled()` / `isSupabaseBrowserSameOrigin()` so HTTPS Tunnel uses `wss://` page origin.
5. Ops truth: `docs/technical/on-prem-pack-install-upgrade.zh.md`

## Pack size / Next caches (hard)

`pack-release` zips **sources only**. Excluding literal `.next` is **not** enough — also exclude `.next-*` (`.next-uat`, `.next-typecheck`, …). After every pack: zip should be ~few MB; if stage still has `apps/web/.next*`, fail (script gate). **Never** scp/hand a hundreds-of-MB zip as an on-prem “source” pack.

## Local `next build` before pack (hard)

`pack-release.sh` only zips sources — **web typecheck/compile runs on the store** during `upgrade.sh --build web`. Lint / `next dev` / Chrome UAT **do not** prove Docker `npm run build -w @mesa/web` will pass.

**Before** `pack-release.sh` or telling Will to upgrade, when the release includes changes under `apps/web/src/app|lib|types`, fonts/`next/font`, `middleware`, or Dockerfile-affecting web code:

1. On the **same commit** that will be packed: `npm run build -w @mesa/web` (or repo `npm run build`) must **pass**.
2. Do not ship a zip whose only verification was `lint` + localhost UAT.

### `next/font/local` trap (caught 2026-08-08 on Pirata)

- Google `next/font` often allows `adjustFontFallback: true`.
- **`next/font/local` only:** `adjustFontFallback?: false | 'Arial' | 'Times New Roman'` — **`true` is a type error** and fails store `next build`.
- Prefer omit the option, or set an allowed string / `false`. Never copy Google-font boolean onto `localFont`.
